WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.290
Every contract ends.

2
00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:02.610
The question is how.

3
00:00:03.295 --> 00:00:04.225
Most end well.

4
00:00:04.475 --> 00:00:05.865
Both sides do their part.

5
00:00:05.975 --> 00:00:06.545
That's performance.

6
00:00:07.528 --> 00:00:08.898
Or one side lets the other

7
00:00:08.748 --> 00:00:10.938
off. Someone new takes over.

8
00:00:11.408 --> 00:00:12.838
A new deal replaces the old

9
00:00:12.688 --> 00:00:14.738
one. Or two debts cancel out.

10
00:00:15.388 --> 00:00:16.758
If you end up owing yourself,

11
00:00:16.608 --> 00:00:17.578
the debt is gone.

12
00:00:17.868 --> 00:00:19.578
And after five years with no

13
00:00:19.428 --> 00:00:20.718
claim, it's gone too.

14
00:00:21.349 --> 00:00:22.999
Sometimes no one is to blame.

15
00:00:23.669 --> 00:00:25.019
The hall burns down before the

16
00:00:24.869 --> 00:00:26.519
concert. That's frustration.

17
00:00:27.329 --> 00:00:28.759
But harder or dearer is not

18
00:00:28.609 --> 00:00:29.079
enough.

19
00:00:29.764 --> 00:00:31.574
And sometimes, someone breaks it.

20
00:00:31.864 --> 00:00:33.414
Late, badly, or not at all.

21
00:00:33.264 --> 00:00:34.034
That's breach.

22
00:00:34.808 --> 00:00:36.058
Then you can claim damages.

23
00:00:36.748 --> 00:00:37.898
Ask the court to make them

24
00:00:37.748 --> 00:00:39.058
do it, or make them stop.

25
00:00:39.388 --> 00:00:40.418
Cancel the deal.

26
00:00:40.268 --> 00:00:41.598
Or hold back payment.

27
00:00:42.327 --> 00:00:43.877
Born. Tested. Ended.

28
00:00:44.007 --> 00:00:45.137
That's the Contract Line.
